A||||30||lowCG||Removing sail panels||||5
Z||000000||lowCG||10-21-1999||09:40 PM||||Has anyone any tips on removing the sail panels from a car?<BR>Found a good pair at a U-pick boneyard last week.||||reg||5
Z||000001||kel||10-22-1999||12:21 AM||||Take a look here:   <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/howto.html" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/howto.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-22-1999||01:25 AM||||Oh my,that's a lot of good info. there.<BR>Thanks,I know that it'll be much easier now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Thomas||10-22-1999||03:24 AM||||Use the Panels from a 84 Fiero.<BR>They made with Glas.<BR>I have done it some years ago.<BR>Only modification you need, you must cut a small chanel to the holes where the bolts go in.<BR>Then use a plastic nut or a nut with a plate and screw it on the bolts at the panel. Now you can use the 84s panel in the later Fieros.<BR>Result : Never scratch, never damaged.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||10-22-1999||12:51 PM||||Ok,I was a bit confused;I had remembered my('87) car's cracked panels flexing,then,last week when I was at the junkyard,I saw a broken('84)panel,all crumbly like safety glass.Hadn't given it much thought,but I'll go and get those '84 panels,the junkyard had 17 Fieros!Not much left though.<BR>Thanks for the tip.||||reg||1
